            <div xml:id="d409">

                <pb facs="0360" n="348" sameAs="frus:frus1942v04/pg348"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">890G.24/36: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Iraq</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Farrell</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Baghdad</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1942-07-02T13:00:00+03:00">July 2, 1942—1
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received 3:37 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>135. My 126 [<hi rendition="#italic">127</hi>], June 22, 1 p.m. Military mission
                    customs exemption question has been referred by Iraqi Ministry of Finance to
                    Ministry of Justice. Latter on advice of its British legal adviser now informs
                    me that Iraqi Government desires to negotiate a convention with the United
                    States Government to serve as legal basis for legislation to authorize customs
                    franchise. Draft is now in preparation. Meanwhile I request Department’s views
                    and instructions.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Farrell</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
